    "restoration_notes": "High-value tropical fruit closely related to rambutan with excellent market potential. Its more open canopy makes it compatible with cacao agroforestry systems. Deep, well-drained soils and careful transplanting are essential for successful establishment. Only elite female trees should be propagated through grafting for commercial production. Provides diversified income while maintaining agroforestry canopy structure. Within FYNOS AI, pulasan is recommended as a complementary productive species rather than a primary native Amazon restoration tree."
